WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.040
Part 1. You will hear a woman asking a friend for advice on travelling by ferry to an island

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:15.440
in Scotland. First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 4.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:54.759
You know when you went to the Shetland Islands last year, Paul, did you go by ferry or did

00:00:54.759 --> 00:01:00.720
you fly? We went by ferry, Tammy. I prefer driving to flying. The journey feels like

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:07.639
part of the holiday. Hmm. Which ferry company did you use? There's only one. It's called

00:01:07.639 --> 00:01:13.959
Northern Ferries. The ferries all leave from Aberdeen. How frequent are they? The service

00:01:13.959 --> 00:01:19.160
is pretty limited. There's only one ferry leaving every evening in summer, anyway. Seven

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:24.959
days a week. I'm not sure about the winter months. They may only run on four or five

00:01:24.959 --> 00:01:33.440
days then. OK, so it's an overnight trip. I quite like that idea. Leaving at night and

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:40.199
waking up as you arrive on the island. Can you remember how much you paid for your tickets?

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:46.919
They were really cheap and four people and a car worked out at just under £250. Really?

00:01:46.919 --> 00:01:53.080
I was expecting it to be more like £400 during the peak season. So was I. It's great

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:59.000
value. It's a good idea to book in advance because I think they get booked up quite quickly,

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:06.519
especially during the school holidays. Yes, I suppose so. I'm just not 100% sure of our

00:02:06.519 --> 00:02:14.440
plans yet. What if I had to cancel? That could be a problem. I don't think it's their policy

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:20.800
to give refunds, just a voucher, which you can use at a later date. But you have to cancel

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:30.600
a month in advance to get that. Right. Well, we need to make up our minds quickly then.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:36.800
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions five

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:37.399
to ten.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:21.440
Now listen and answer questions five to ten.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:30.880
You'd want to book a cabin too. We booked too late to get a cabin with a window. They're

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:36.160
more expensive but much nicer than the inner cabins. You don't have to book a cabin at

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:42.240
all but I think it's worth paying for. They also have luxury cabins which are only for

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:48.960
two people and have a TV. But I wouldn't bother with those. No, I agree. The only other

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:54.360
thing I can think of is to make sure you bring snacks for the kids. The selection on board

00:03:54.360 --> 00:04:03.039
is quite limited and not that healthy either. What about Wi-Fi on board? Is that any good?

00:04:03.039 --> 00:04:09.199
Not really. So it's best to bring some books for them. OK. We may need to bring the dog

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:14.839
if I can't get anyone to look after him. We brought ours and it was fine. The kennels

00:04:14.839 --> 00:04:22.040
on board are OK. They're quite big. You just need to provide a blanket. Sounds good. It

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:27.679
was all very easy really and it was quite an adventure for the kids. They loved being

00:04:27.679 --> 00:04:34.079
on the sea at night and in the morning keeping a lookout for dolphins. We saw loads. Oh,

00:04:34.079 --> 00:04:39.839
the kids would love that. One other thing. We arrived in Aberdeen hours before the ferry

00:04:39.839 --> 00:04:44.799
was due to leave so we decided to go somewhere else rather than hang around at the port for

00:04:44.799 --> 00:04:52.640
so long. Where did you go? Drum Castle. I've never heard of it. Is that spelt like the

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:59.079
instrument? Yeah. It's really worth visiting. It's got an impressive tower and beautiful

00:04:59.119 --> 00:05:06.119
gardens and ancient woodland. Sounds lovely. Does it have a restaurant? It's only got a

00:05:06.119 --> 00:05:12.200
coffee shop, no restaurant. We looked up restaurants in the area and found an Italian one in a

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:19.200
village nearby. I can check the name of it for you if you're interested. Oh, thanks Paul.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:28.559
That is the end of part one. You now have one minute to check your answers to part one.

